5. CRUD Operations

| **Object**       | **Create(POST)**                        | **Read(GET)**         | **Update(PUT)**              | **Delete(DELETE)**      |
| **Users**        | Register new learner/assessor           | Profile fetch         | Update profile/settings      | Account deletion        |
| **Tasks**        | Add new task	                         | Fetch learner tasks   | Mark complete/update status  | Remove task             |
| **Progress**     | Auto-generated	                         | View progress summary | Update after task completion | N/A (system-managed)    |
| **Bookings**     | Submit booking	                         | View bookings	       | Confirm/reschedule/decline	  | Cancel booking          |
| **Challenges**   | System adds	                         | Fetch challenge	 | Submit answer	              | N/A                     |
| **Leaderboard**  | Auto-update	                         | View leaderboard	 | Update XP/rank	              | N/A                     |



6. Validation Rules

- Email format must match regex ^[^@]+@[^@]+\.[^@]+$.
- Password minimum 8 characters, must include uppercase, lowercase, number.
- Dates must be valid ISO YYYY-MM-DD.
- Booking times must be within working hours (08:00–18:00).
- XP updates only allowed via challenge completion.

7. Security Approach

Authentication: Firebase Auth with email/password, optional 2FA.

Authorization:
* Learners can only access their own tasks, progress, bookings.
* Assessors can view learners they are assigned to, manage bookings.
* Assessors have full access.

Firestore Rules:
* match /users/{userId} { allow read, update: if request.auth.uid == userId }
* match /tasks/{taskId} { allow read: if request.auth.uid == resource.data.learnerId }
* match /bookings/{bookingId} { allow update: if request.auth.uid == resource.data.assessorId }
